   "text": "count from the end, so \"python\"[-1] is \"n\". Slicing \"python\"[1:4] returns \"yth\" (start included, stop excluded).  F-strings embed expressions inside text: f\"Total: {price * 2:.2f}\" formats a number with two decimals. Integer division // discards the fractional part (7 // 2 is 3), the modulo operator % returns the remainder (7 % 2 is 1), and ** is exponentiation (2 ** 10 is 1024). Dividing with / always returns a float, so 6 / 3 is 2.0.",
